WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.550
This film shows how to report an
incident, and how officers respond.

2
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.520
Warning.

3
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:11.467
If a person is in danger, call 911 first.

4
00:00:11.517 --> 00:00:15.040
To make a report, select
Report an incident.

5
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:21.010
Then select a method: Report by
voice, Guided form, or Quick alert.

6
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.540
For a report by voice,
select Start talking.

7
00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.940
Select Start voice interview.

8
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.940
Then allow the microphone.

9
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.550
The interviewer speaks first.

10
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.690
Interviewer: Hi, you've reached
the Downtown safety line.

11
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:36.940
Interviewer: What happened?

12
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:37.740
Caller: Hi.

13
00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:42.430
Caller: A man is pulling on car door
handles on South Second Street, right now.

14
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.920
Interviewer: Is anyone hurt,
and did you see a weapon?

15
00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.360
Answer in your own words.

16
00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.920
It asks one short question at a
time, and you can interrupt it.

17
00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.240
When it has the facts, it fills
in the report on your screen.

18
00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.090
Then select Review and submit.

19
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.980
The guided form has five short steps.

20
00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.620
First, select what is happening.

21
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.580
If it is happening now, set the switch.

22
00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.140
Also set a switch if you saw a
weapon, or if a person is hurt.

23
00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:19.020
Next, show the place: your
business, or a pin on the map.

24
00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.140
Then describe each person or vehicle.

25
00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:27.100
In Details, type what happened,
or select Dictate and speak.

26
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.380
Organize my notes fills
in the fields for you.

27
00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:33.230
Then select Review report.

28
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.160
If there is no time, use a quick alert.

29
00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.840
Select what is happening.

30
00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.800
Then select Send alert now.

31
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:46.170
Officers and nearby businesses
get the alert at once.

32
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.580
Before you send, check the report.

33
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:54.567
The dashboard suggests a
priority, from P1 to P4.

34
00:01:54.617 --> 00:01:57.287
Alert nearby businesses is on.

35
00:01:57.337 --> 00:02:00.460
For officers only, set it to off.

36
00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:04.220
Officers may contact me
lets an officer call you.

37
00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.620
Select Send to officers.

38
00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.100
You hear the report read back.

39
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:14.670
In My reports, follow each status,
from Received to Resolved.

40
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:20.640
Officers see each new report at
once, in the Operations Center.

41
00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:23.520
The most urgent reports are at the top.

42
00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:27.920
With Voice alerts on, the
dashboard reads new reports aloud.

43
00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:30.360
Select a report to open it.

44
00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.000
Select Acknowledge.

45
00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:35.547
The reporter then sees Seen by officers.

46
00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:38.720
When you go to the place,
select Responding.

47
00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:42.827
Add a note: internal, or
visible to the reporter.

48
00:02:42.877 --> 00:02:47.147
To warn others about a person
or a vehicle, select BOLO.

49
00:02:47.197 --> 00:02:49.840
When you finish, select Resolve.

50
00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.360
Select an outcome.

51
00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:54.210
Then select Mark resolved.

52
00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:56.720
Report what you see.

53
00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.640
Officers respond.

54
00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.410
Scan the code to make a report.
